    irada: 'Pattern teeno peedhiyon me <b>anjaane</b> me chala: na saas ne, na Usha ne, na Pallavi ne ise soch kar chuna. Is episode me naya hai <b>awareness</b>: Pallavi ab pattern ko pehchanti hai, isliye use chunna band kar sakti hai. Usha bhi pehle defensive autopilot par jaati hain, phir ek seedhe, bina ilzaam wale sawaal se apni kahani bata paati hain. Badlav ek baar ka faisla nahi; stress me purana pattern phir aayega, aur har baar use pehchanna hi practice hai.',
    gap: 'Counsellor ke paas jaane se pehle bhi Pallavi jaanti thi ki chup ho jaana theek nahi. Par jaankari se aadat nahi badalti: stress ke pal me dimaag sabse purana, sabse zyada practice kiya hua raasta pakadta hai. Badlav ke liye chahiye pehle se tayyar shabd, ek insaan jo pyaar se yaad dilaye, aur galti hone par khud ko maaf karke phir se koshish.',
    real: ['Lieberman aur saathi (2007): "Putting feelings into words"', 'UCLA ke is fMRI study me participants ne gusse ya dar wale chehron ki tasveer dekh kar kabhi emotion ka naam chuna ("angry", "scared"), kabhi koi aur match kiya. Emotion ka naam chunne par amygdala ki activity kam aur prefrontal cortex ke ek hisse ki activity zyada dikhi. Ye ek chhota lab study hai aur asli rishton par seedha laagu nahi hota; par "naam dene se feeling thodi kaabu me aati hai" wala idea kai therapies me bhi istemaal hota hai.'],
